1. **Trim restated inference only.** In ch16 after "*He needs a crowd*", and in ch18 around the continuous declaration, the attention toll and late-day fatigue, a conclusion arrives three times: scene, Cael's thought, binder entry. Cut one of the three where the evidence has already landed. Keep every failed method, test, counterexample, binder artifact and the full Seln viewpoint. Leave the fights alone.
2. **Orient the measurement vocabulary once** (ch20 seeding; ch21 Bracken on standings and squad selection). Add or sharpen one plain sentence separating permanent formal classification (Path tier and rank) from seasonal standing (ladder position, seed, crown, squad). Use no exposition block.

